C MP+relaxed
"Relaxed message passing, outcome r0=1 /\ r1=0 (flag seen set, data stale). The
 Relaxed Memory Calculus (RMC) specifies ordering DIRECTLY in the source with
 explicit visibility (VEDGE / vo) and execution (XEDGE / xo) edges rather than
 per-access memory-order annotations. The RMC author would place a VEDGE from the
 data write to the flag write and an XEDGE on the reader, which together FORBID
 this stale-data outcome. Plain C11 with all-RELAXED atomics (no such edges)
 ALLOWS it: relaxed accesses carry no happens-before. herd7 -c11 => Sometimes.
 RMC has no herd7 model (it is a source-level calculus), so its forbidding
 verdict is cited; the C11 verdict is machine-run. OOTA does NOT separate the two
 (RMC also permits thin-air). The reverse direction -- RMC is 'strictly more
 relaxed than any existing architecture' and admits leapfrogging/forwarding
 speculation C11 has no mode to express -- is a model-level claim with no single
 canonical litmus. See README."
{ int x=0; int f=0; }
P0 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* f) {
  atomic_store_explicit(x,1,memory_order_relaxed);
  atomic_store_explicit(f,1,memory_order_relaxed);
}
P1 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* f) {
  int r0 = atomic_load_explicit(f,memory_order_relaxed);
  int r1 = atomic_load_explicit(x,memory_order_relaxed);
}
exists (1:r0=1 /\ 1:r1=0)
